      "notes": [
        {
          "text": "Kamarajar Port Limited's consolidated Scale of Rates has no overall effective date; the latest amendment to vessel-related charges is for container vessels from 4 June 2019, and the latest amendment of any kind is from July 2025. No 2026 revision was found, so these rates may be out of date.",
          "source": {
            "document": "sor-consolidated",
            "page": 1
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Pilotage rates are per GT by size band with no statement that they apply incrementally, so the whole tonnage is charged at its band's rate.",
          "source": {
            "document": "sor-consolidated",
            "page": 6
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "The berth hire table covers coal berths, the general cargo berth and finger jetties. Container vessels at the BOT container terminals are not covered by it, so container berth hire is not priced.",
          "source": {
            "document": "sor-consolidated",
            "page": 7
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "The two one-page annexes (coastal cars, granite blocks) are cargo promotions and are not entered.",
          "source": {
            "document": "sor-annex-2",
            "page": 1
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Dry bulk ships at anchorage pay nothing for the first 48 hours, then per GT: Rs. 0.023 / US$ 0.001 from 49 to 96 hours, Rs. 0.046 / US$ 0.002 from 97 to 144 hours and Rs. 0.092 / US$ 0.004 beyond 144 hours. The table doesn't say whether this is per hour or for the whole period, so anchorage is not priced.",
          "source": {
            "document": "sor-consolidated",
            "page": 8,
            "section": "5"
          }
        }
      ]
